  "body": "https://url.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/5fc4c4c17f3077beda5e3647df73f4b1b0ba7084/#url-representation\r\n\r\nThe URL spec is exporting a bunch of terms relating to parts of a URL. This is fine, but some of them are a bit too generic and end up creating auto-linking conflicts. It would be helpful if e.g. `A URL’s <dfn export>fragment</dfn>` were written as `A URL’s <dfn lt=\"URL fragment\" local-lt=\"fragment\" export>fragment</dfn>` so that the exported term includes the word “URL”. (The local-lt attribute allows the unqualified term to be used within the URL spec itself.)",
